==English==

===Etymology===
Usually said to allude to the fact that an affected person is frequently running to get to a toilet immediately. Sometimes said to allude to [[Bristol stool chart|the runniness (runny consistency) of the stool]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹʌnz/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-runs.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌnz|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{head|en|noun form}}

# {{plural of|en|run}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|p}}

# {{lb|en|slang|often with "the"}} [[diarrhea|Diarrhea]]/[[diarrhoea]].
#: {{syn|en|the shits}}
#: {{ux|en|He missed several days of school because he had '''the runs'''. They think it was a Norovirus infection.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=Joseph A. Petak|title=Never Plan Tomorrow: The Saga of the Bataan Death March and Battle of Corregidor Survivors 1942-1945
|text=We also had a bad case of '''runs''' since we were not used to the rich meat.}}

====Synonyms====
* (''diarrh(o)ea''): diarrhea/diarrhoea, the [[squits]] {{qualifier|slang}}, the [[trots]] {{qualifier|slang}}, the [[craps]] {{qualifier|slang}}, [[the squirts]] {{qualifier|slang}}

